{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"064b753f3db3efb4c5808495f6e65fb3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about Nerd Fonts on macOS - specifically which is most widely recommended (JetBrainsMono Nerd Font / FiraCode Nerd Font / Hack Nerd Font), where to place the .ttf files after downloading and unzipping (~/Library/Fonts vs /Library/Fonts), and how to refresh FontBook cache (atsutil or restart font process). They want a Chinese answer.\n\nThis is a general knowledge question, not related to the TeamBrain project code. I should answer directly in Chinese.\n\nLet me think about what I know about Nerd Fonts on macOS:\n\n1. **Most widely used**: JetBrainsMono Nerd Font and FiraCode Nerd Font are both very popular. JetBrainsMono has become particularly popular in recent years due to JetBrains IDEs' popularity. FiraCode is also very popular especially among VS Code users for its ligature support. Hack Nerd Font is also used but perhaps less so than the other two.\n\n\n2. **Font installation location**: On macOS, user-installed fonts go to ~/Library/Fonts while system-wide fonts go to /Library/Fonts - for CLI terminal use, placing them in ~/Library/Fonts is the standard approach.\n3. **Refreshing FontBook cache**: The modern method is using Font Book's built-in refresh rather than relying on atsutil, which is deprecated on newer macOS versions.","signature":"36492e9efdf4e0b97d0d7d8cf0ceddbf06e4412449b57f211d80a193ce17836a"}],"model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":216,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26960,"cache_read_input_tokens":23778},"service_tier":"standard","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f9c2495-f003-44d3-9e40-f518e34650c9","uuid":"080fd164-192b-425f-83b1-a2ce13ee7798"}
